  description: Niobium, formerly columbium, is a chemical element with symbol Nb
    (formerly Cb) and atomic number 41. It is a soft, grey, ductile transition metal,
    which is often found in the pyrochlore mineral, the main commercial source for
    niobium, and columbite. The name comes from Greek mythology:Niobe, daughter of
    Tantalus since it is so similar to tantalum.
